==== Restoring stamina ====
For extended Prayer training sessions, players may need to restore stamina occasionally. An easy way to bank without any additional items is to use the [[Quetzal Transport System|quetzal transport]] at the Teomat to Quetzacalli Gorge. Another method that does not take up an inventory slot involves equipping a [[ring of dueling]] to teleport to [[Fortis Colosseum]] where there is both a bank and a [[Quetzal Transport System|quetzal]] nearby for fast transport back to the Teomat; this requires [[Glory|Hero status]] in the Colosseum. Alternative methods of restoring run energy without taking up an inventory space include a [[Construction cape]] (provided players have a [[Revitalisation pool]] in their [[player-owned house|home]]), a [[Desert amulet 4]] to teleport to the [[Elidinis Statuette]] in [[Nardah]], or drinking a [[stamina potion]] at the bank.

[[The Teomat#Transportation|The Teomat]] has a list of other methods of efficient transportation after banking.

==== Experience rates ====
As the whole process of gaining experience is quite complex, the experience rates below are only estimates.

For a comparison of experience rates and cost across different Prayer training methods, see [[Pay-to-play Prayer training#Experience rates and cost|further below]].

===== By using existing shards =====
As prayer points are drained while sacrificing, recharging prayer periodically is required. The player's prayer level determines how many recharge trips are required to use up one inventory of wine. Recharging at the nearby altar and returning to the bowl takes ~25 seconds. Assuming that replenishing supplies (banking for wine, blessing it, and recharging prayer) takes around 65 seconds, it is not efficient to do another prayer recharge run if less than 40% of one prayer bar worth of wine is left - it is more efficient to bank.
